 Quick prototyping – Easier to implement in test code for basic communication.
 * When: You need high-speed communication (e.g., >400 kHz I²C, high-speed UART/SPI).
 The CPU is already heavily loaded — bit banging is CPU-intensive.
 Power efficiency is a priority — more CPU cycles = more power.
 Timing accuracy is critical (e.g., real-time systems).
 Your application demands robust, reliable communication under load.*/

